    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="1313" n="1307" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1307"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                                1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith the final
                    correspondence touching the attitude of the diplomatic agent of the United
                    States in regard to the use <pb facs="1314" n="1308" xml:id="pg1308"/> of force,
                    being two letters from Hon. S. B. Dole, minister of foreign affairs, dated
                    February 5 and February 14, 1894, and my reply thereto, dated February 14,
                    1894.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister
                            Plenipotentiary,<lb/>United States of America.</hi></signed></closer>




